  "settled_contracts": [
    "R2245/R2417 bind matching Workflow Run\u2194Workflow, Step Run\u2194Step and Action Run\u2194Action; each Run-kind Draft specifies one outgoing IS_EXECUTION_OF and each definition Draft separately allows zero or more outgoing HAS_EXECUTION.",
    "R2246/R2421 bind Event Record\u2192Event and its derived reverse; R2557 bounds each record to exactly one outgoing RECORDS and R2755 separately allows Event zero or more IS_RECORDED_BY.",
    "R2255/R2420 bind Runtime\u2192Execution and its derived reverse; R2753 allows Runtime zero or more EXECUTES, R2749 allows each Execution one or more IS_EXECUTED_BY.",
    "R2760/R2761 bind Execution\u2192Event and derived reverse; R2749 allows zero or more PRODUCES and R2755 requires one or more IS_PRODUCED_BY. No upper one follows on those reverse counts.",
    "R2465 retains the existing Step choice between running one Action/Workflow and containing one or more Substeps; R2464 and R2467 retain their existing independent Relation allowances."
  ],
  "atomic_gates": [
    "The eleven proposed Occurrent/Execution/Run/Runtime/Event kind Drafts R2749\u2013R2759 must be independently accepted with the eight paired relation Declarations and the four endpoint Declarations; none of those Drafts is Current authority until adopted.",
    "Reconcile and review the corrected R2557 and R2255 previews with their exact native Drafts, preserve unchanged Summaries, and refresh source/version pins before any adoption. R2582/R2583/Event Record author representation and any additional Actor-side reverse permission require separate effective-authority verification.",
    "Check default-zero inheritance and named outgoing permissions on both written directions independently for selected model and instance layers. The signature and HAS_INVERSE binding do not grant inverse permission.",
    "Coordinate newly settled Atom.Header.Container source/schema changes with affected Atom endpoint Headers and avoid duplicating storage; current +>/<+ and named Relation syntax remain in force until A1321 source adoption.",
    "Assign versions against all same-ID Current/Draft/Archive history, preserve exact preimages and adopt mutually dependent source changes together; regenerate the source frontier and projections after acceptance.",
    "No actual O Workflow definitions, runtime/data, code, tests, Git or Current/Draft sources were changed.",
    "Integrate the newly accepted :: and {::n} spelling consistently with its reviewed source grammar and all coupled candidates, without altering any Relation cardinality or binding. Current source syntax remains the executable/readback baseline until that source authority is adopted."
  ],
  "open_question": null,
  "qualification": "R2557 author allowance is supported by the required R2582 relation-field cardinality and R2583 endpoint signature; the separately reviewed preview preserves that exact one-Actor value per Event Record. This does not grant a reverse direction.",
